Add an 'environment_indicator_navigation' submodule that shows the active
environment as a coloured stripe along the inline-start edge of the core
Navigation sidebar, the way the module already colours Gin's vertical toolbar.

Under core Navigation the module's full-width 'page_top' strip renders beneath
the fixed sidebar and top bar, where nothing can see it, while still occupying
its height in the document flow. The submodule reduces that strip to its
attachments, which keeps the favicon colouring working.

Navigation support is tracked upstream at
https://www.drupal.org/project/environment_indicator/issues/3457688 but is not
in any release: 'modules/' on both the 4.x and 5.0.x branches contains only
'environment_indicator_toolbar' and 'environment_indicator_ui'. Because this
patch only adds files, it will fail to apply the moment a release ships its own
submodule of this name - which is the signal to drop the patch. Note that the
upstream design renders a named button rather than a stripe, so the two are not
visually equivalent.

