+# Environment Indicator - Navigation Integration
+
+Shows the active environment as a coloured stripe along the inline-start edge
+of the core Navigation sidebar, the way the parent module colours Gin's
+vertical toolbar.
+
+Enabling this module also removes the parent module's full-width `page_top`
+strip. Under core Navigation that strip renders beneath the fixed sidebar and
+top bar, where it cannot be seen, while still occupying its height in the
+document flow. The favicon colouring the strip carries is preserved.
+
+## Appearance
+
+The stripe takes the active environment's `bg_color`, so it reads the same way
+the rest of the module does - one colour per environment. Two custom
+properties control it:
+
+| Property | Default | Set by |
+|----------|---------|--------|
+| `--environment-indicator-navigation-color` | `transparent` | The module, from `environment_indicator.indicator` `bg_color` |
+| `--environment-indicator-navigation-width` | `8px` | Override in a theme to change the thickness |
+
+## Visibility
+
+The stripe is drawn only for users holding both `access environment indicator`
+and `access navigation`, and only when an environment name is configured. A
+user who can see the indicator but not the navigation keeps the parent
+module's strip, which nothing covers for them.
+
+## Upstream
+
+Navigation support for Environment Indicator is tracked at
+https://www.drupal.org/project/environment_indicator/issues/3457688. Once a
+release ships its own `environment_indicator_navigation` submodule, drop the
+patch that provides this one and use the released module instead. Note that
+the upstream design renders a named button in the sidebar rather than a
+stripe, so the two are not visually equivalent.
